From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:13:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: report the frame exposure on T8132

T8132 reports each frame's gain and exposure time in the fourth section
of its frame metadata, like T6040 and T8140. Measured on the J604 with
apple_isp.unverified_meta_exposure set: in a dim room auto exposure
lengthened the exposure from 20 ms to 30 ms, inside the 33.3 ms frame
period at 30 frames per second, and raised the gain from 3.6 to 12.2
times unity within two seconds, which is the convergence the report
describes on the other SoCs.

Give T8132 meta_exposure, so it gets the read-only gain and exposure
controls by default. The parameter stays for SoCs whose layout is not
yet measured.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
index ce24b26f5e..bce76037d4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
@@ -1299,7 +1299,7 @@ static const struct apple_isp_hw apple_isp_hw_t8132 = {
 	.shared_size = 0xdec00000,
 	.fw_restore = true,
 	.deferred_start = true,
-	.meta_exposure_unverified = true,
+	.meta_exposure = true,
 };
 
